# observatory-workspace.ux.nt — the MINIMAL sux:Workspace seed for a graph whose
# center pane is a layout-document dashboard (first tenant: the `observatory`
# graph on the cloud-2 canary).
#
# APPLIED AT SEED TIME, NOT BUILD TIME: these triples are inserted into the
# observatory cell's `:ux:config` named graph
# (`urn:mnemosyne:local:graph:{graph_id}:ux:config`) as a DEPLOY step — e.g. an
# `rdf_load` with target_graph_iri set to that slot, the same mechanism the
# garden-default gateway seed uses. The organism build never embeds this file;
# the hosted shell READS it back through the normal live-read path
# (loadConfigFromCell -> parseNT -> parseTriplesToConfig -> validateConfig).
#
# Shape (proven by apps/organism/src/cell/observatory-workspace-seed.test.ts):
#   - region-top-bar   chrome root (mn-top-bar) — workspace switcher/auth chrome.
#   - region-center    THE FRAGMENT MARKER: renderedByComponent
#                      "sh-layout-dashboard" declares "this region's subtree is
#                      a graph-authored layout fragment". The Surface path
#                      SPLICES the fragment's ux:layoutJson LayoutDocument into
#                      the ONE workspace Surface document (Surface unification,
#                      docs/design/surface-unification.md); the shell loads and
#                      persists it (cell/workspace-fragments.ts). This region
#                      carries NO sux:fragmentSurface, so the shell applies the
#                      default surface IRI below — deliberate back-compat: this
#                      exact seed predates the predicate and is live on canary.
#   - region-right-rail optional stacked chat rail (panel-chat/mn-chat-panel);
#                      collapsed by default in the shell until panels are opened.
#   - NO file-tree/sidebar dependency: the observatory graph has no documents to
#     browse, so no region docks mn-sidebar-panel.
#
# The fragment's CONTENT (the ux:layoutJson layout-document literal) lives in
# the same :ux:config slot under <urn:sophia:ux:surface:observatory-dashboard>
# and is authored/persisted separately; with no ux:layoutJson present the shell
# loads the canned observatory v0 fallback for this default surface (only).
#
# The same subject may ALSO carry an OPTIONAL sibling ux:vegaTheme literal —
# a partial Vega-Lite chart-theme override merged over the in-repo default
# theme (packages/runtime/src/editor-services/vega-theme.ts). No graph needs
# one: the in-repo default already makes every chart.vega-lite cell in the
# canned dashboard conform, light and dark, with zero graph authoring. See
# observatory-vega-theme.README.md (this directory) for the full convention.
